Quality Manager
Novitex Enterprise Solutions, formerly Pitney Bowes Management Services, delivers innovative document and communications management solutions that help companies around the world drive business process efficiencies, increase productivity, reduce costs and improve customer satisfaction. For almost 30 years, clients have turned to us to integrate and optimize their enterprise-wide business processes to empower employees, increase productivity and maximize results. As a trusted partner, we continually focus on delivering secure, technology-enabled document and communications solutions that improve our clients' work processes, enhance their customer interactions and drive growth.
The Quality Manager will be based in our Phoenix, AZ client location. The purpose of this position is to ensure that the products and/or services are consistent and meets both external and internal requirements; to monitor and advise on the performance of the quality management system, produce data and report on performance, measuring against set standards; to manage and recommend processes improvements; to provides training, tools and techniques to enable others to achieve quality. 
 Responsibilities: 
 Establish/Monitor quality procedures, standards, and specifications; 
 Review customer requirements and ensure that they are met; 
 Work with purchasing to establish quality requirements from external suppliers, as necessary; 
 Set and Manage standards for quality as well as safety; 
 Ensure production and related processes meet international and national standards; 
 Define quality procedures in conjunction with operating staff; 
 Monitor performance, gather data and produce statistical reports and advise/assist in the achievement of goals; 
 Support the Quality Management System; 
 Participate in the Corrective and Preventative Action process; 
 Assist in the development of procedures, work instructions and quality system documents in accordance with established standards; 
 Establish and implement the necessary communication strategy for the improvement and awareness of quality issues (including any relevant standard changes) across all departments. 
 Liaise and cooperate with quality management and standards bodies. 
 Liaise and communicate with vendors and customers where necessary. 
 Coach and develop site QA/QC team 
 Perform due diligence as required for prospective opportunities.
TECHNICAL QUALIFICATIONS: 
 Must possess excellent written / verbal communication skills 
 Proficient in PC operations, MS Office applications. 
 Familiarity with database queries and reports. 
 Quality systems experience, ISO Preferable. 
 Lean and/or Six Sigma experience, desirable 
 EXPERIENCE: 
 Manufacturing background desirable. 
 Printing and/or Document Management background desirable. 
 EDUCATIONAL REQUIREMENT: 
 High School Diploma required, College degree preferred and / or 5-7 years in a Quality Management Role

